-- title:
--   Level automorphisms generate a group of order dividing ℓ-1
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and assume there is a ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota_0(\zeta)=e^{2\pi i/q}$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ (using $\ell\mid q^2M'$). Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((X))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) attached to the congruence subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $G\le\mathrm{Aut}_L(K)$ be the subgroup generated by those $\tau$ for which there exists $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), i.e. $\tau$ realises the slash action of the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}a&b/q\\ qc&d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}$ on all quotients $f/g$ of $q$-expansions of weight-$k$ modular forms for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions, after applying any ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Then $G$ is finite and $\#G$ divides $\ell-1$.
--
--   The statement bounds the Galois-theoretic size of the group of level automorphisms of the auxiliary function field of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ (full level $q$, $\Gamma_0$ at $M'$, trivial determinant character at $\ell$): the automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ act through the diamond operators at $\ell$, whose group has order dividing $\ell-1$. It feeds the finiteness and orbit arguments on the auxiliary level-one charts of the full-level modular curve.
